    "salt": "QQ5vOaoAM3Q3dwkFC8OEcw==",
    "text": "Emer, also called Eimher and Emer of the Fair Hair, is an Irish heroine. She became the wife of the great hero Cúchulainn. For nearly two thousand years her name meant the ideal of womanhood. Christian monks transcribed the Ulster Cycle and may have shaped her as a model wife. Emer was loyal and never jealous. She died with Cúchulainn at the last. Her father was Forgall Monach, who at first refused the match. He shut the hero in the fortress at Lusca, now Lusk. Cúchulainn sprang free with a great salmon leap and killed many men. He carried Emer, with gold and silver, to his home at Dún Delgan. Only the fairy queen Fand troubled her. When the lovers parted, the pair swallowed a draught that washed away all memory.",
